    "report_narrative": "Compared to last report: Most major fertilizers have increased in price slightly. Widespread rainfall across Oklahoma over the past 30 days has significantly improved wheat pasture, resulting in increased demand for fertilizer. Rising costs of key production inputs used in manufacturing DAP and MAP continue to drive fertilizer production costs higher. These escalating expenses have placed additional financial pressure on manufacturers, reportedly leading at least one U.S. production facility to idle operations. Fuel prices have continued to trend higher over the past 60 days, with farm diesel increasing $0.82 per gallon and propane rising $0.29 per gallon during this period. These higher fuel costs continue to add to operating expenses for agricultural producers.",
